ArgoCD on Local/AWS:

- Create an EC2 instance, allocate 20GB
- connect with SSH on macbook Terminal

** Setup & Installation **

pre-requisites: 
1.Docker(it needs permission to run/access) which I have already done
2.Kind(kubernetes in Docker)
3.Kubectl
4.Helm (you can install ArgoCD using Helm or cube kubectl)
⭐️Helm is used in Production(recommended)

create KIND-Config file(vim KIND-Config.yaml)- this is a manifest file (This create's a kind cluster)

*** Installation of ArgoCD ***

1) kubectl create namespace argocd
2) kubectl apply -n argocd --server-side --force-conflicts -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/argoproj/argo-cd/stable/manifests/install.yaml
refer this documentation: https://argo-cd.readthedocs.io/en/stable/getting_started/

To Set the argocd as default namespace use the following command
-kubectl config set-context --current --namespace=argocd

- Run argocd on kubernetes cluster, by creating a namespace with the name argocd.
command: kubectl create namespace argocd

- Then, port forwarding it to a free port 8080 or 8081 or any other as you like.
command: kubectl port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8081:443

- To login first time using the password which would be saved in the kubernetes sercrets, it will be encrypted(Opaque). use the following command to get the password
command: kubectl -n argocd get secret argocd-initial-admin-secret \
          -o jsonpath="{.data.password}" | base64 -d; echo

Login and Update password. Enjoy using ArgoCD

When done with the argocd work/tasks, kill the process to forcefully stop/end the process using the following command
command: kill -9 $(lsof -t -i:8081)
note: use the exact port number to kill the process accordingly in the above command.

